{title: 47 Por la mañana}
{key: D}
{capo: 1}
{time: 6/8}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts, 1719 (1674-1748); Vers. esp.: Francisco H. Westphal (1858-1944)}
{composer: Aaron Williams, 1762 (1731-1776)}

{sov}
[D]Por la[A] ma[D]ña[Bm]na, ¡oh[D] Se[A]ñor!,
[D]elevo[A] a[E] ti mi[A] voz;
[D]a[G] tu buen[A] nombre[D] doy lo[G]or
[D]con gra[A]ti[D]tud, mi Dios.
{eov}

{sov}
[D]El sol[A] bri[D]llan[Bm]te ya[D] sa[A]lió,
[D]camino[A] en[E] su[A] luz;
[D]del Sal[G]va[A]dor es[D] símbo[G]lo,
[D]del magno[A] Rey, Je[D]sús.
{eov}

{sov}
[D]Los ciel[A]os[D] cuen[Bm]tan al[D] que[A] cree
[D]la gloria[A] del[E] Se[A]ñor;
[D]la lla[G]ma a[A]vivan[D] de la[G] fe
[D]y alien[A]tan el[D] amor.
{eov}

{sov}
[D]En la[A] ma[D]ña[Bm]na eterna[D], pues[A],
[D]contigo[A] cuan[E]do es[A]té,
[D]yo del[G] Cor[A]dero[D] y de Moi[G]sés
